Trying to format JavaScript code inside an cshtml page(within a @section Scripts tag) causes the formatting to behave incorrectly.
Example code:

```
@section Scripts {
    &lt;script&gt;
        const messageTemplate = @Json.Serialize(L["whatsapp_template"]);
        const kindTexts = {
            a5: @Json.Serialize(L["wa_kind_a5"]),
            six: @Json.Serialize(L["wa_kind_six"])
        };
        const copiesTexts = {
            "3": @Json.Serialize(L["wa_copies_3"]),
            "2": @Json.Serialize(L["wa_copies_2"])
        };
        const qtyTexts = {
            one: @Json.Serialize(L["wa_qty_one"]),
            few: @Json.Serialize(L["wa_qty_few"]),
            many: @Json.Serialize(L["wa_qty_many"]),
            other: @Json.Serialize(L["wa_qty_other"])
        };
    &lt;/script&gt;
}
```

Pressing the format document option either from Edit-&gt;Advanced-&gt;Format Document, or via the hotkeys i.e, Ctrl+K, Ctrl+D causes the closing curly braces to move to the right each time the option is pressed. Example outcome for the "copiesTexts" constant:

```
const copiesTexts = {
    "3": @Json.Serialize(L["wa_copies_3"]),
    "2": @Json.Serialize(L["wa_copies_2"])
        };
```

Pressing it again:

```
const copiesTexts = {
    "3": @Json.Serialize(L["wa_copies_3"]),
    "2": @Json.Serialize(L["wa_copies_2"])
                };
```

It repeats every time it is pressed. This seems to happen when there is a mix of C# and Javascript from my observations.

